OpenJDK (default-jre-headless)
  License: GPL-2.0 WITH Classpath-exception-2.0
  Source: Debian bookworm package
  Why this is acceptable: the Classpath exception removes the copyleft effect
  for the common case. This is an aggregation, not a combined work. See
  docs/DATACARD.md §1 and SPEC.md §5.6.

Debian base image userland (bash, coreutils, sed, tar, grep, ...)
  License: GPL-2.0 / GPL-3.0-or-later
  Why this is acceptable: these are AGGREGATED in the image, not combined into
  our application, and we do not depend on their core functionality. The literal
  requirement "no GPL in the image" is IMPOSSIBLE to satisfy — every Debian or
  Ubuntu image contains GPL binaries. See docs/DATACARD.md §1 for the actual
  policy we apply, and note that the wording of that policy still needs legal
  review (SPEC.md §13.5).

