DELIBERATELY NOT INCLUDED
================================================================================

GATK4
  License: Apache-2.0 (the toolkit itself)
  NOT SHIPPED, on purpose. Its official runtime pulls in proprietary Intel
  oneMKL, GPL R/GSL, and LGPL htsjdk-tribble (which cannot be stripped).
  Replacing it with FreeBayes removed all three problems at once.
  We also found that GATK4's own POM describes htsjdk-tribble as MIT while the
  artifact is LGPL-2.1 — i.e. the metadata is wrong. Do not trust POM license
  fields; open the artifact.
  Separately: GATK3 is the non-commercial trap in this family. GATK4 >= 4.2 is
  Apache-2.0, but GATK3 is not. Do not substitute one for the other.

libgsl / gsl-bin / r-base
  License: GPL-3.0-or-later / GPL-2.0-or-later
  Excluded: would make downstream tools GPL-governed. The build gate fails if
  libgsl appears in the dependency tree.

dbNSFP and derived in-silico predictors (REVEL, CADD, PolyPhen-2, AlphaMissense, ...)
  License: CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, with a paid commercial tier
  Excluded from the T2 dataset: the ND clause forbids derivatives, and the NC
  clause forbids commercial use. Turning a source into a test item IS a
  derivative, so ND content is unusable here regardless of the NC question.

SpliceAI annotations inside gnomAD releases
  License: CC BY-NC 4.0
  Excluded: any gnomAD file containing the SpliceAI column was dropped whole.
  Note the main gnomAD data is CC0-1.0 — only the SpliceAI column is NC.

OMIM / GeneReviews
  License: third-party copyright, redistribution restricted.
  Excluded.

